msgid "Quantum optimization {#quantum-optimization}"
msgstr "Optimisasi kuantum {#quantum-optimization}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum optimization explores how quantum computing can be used to solve optimization problems, where the goal is to find the best, or a good, solution among many possible alternatives (often under a set of constraints). Applications of this field include logistics and scheduling, portfolio optimization, and protein folding.\n"
"Quantum optimization approaches include quantum approximate optimization algorithms (QAOA) and other hybrid quantum-classical methods that combine quantum processors with classical optimization techniques. Although quantum computing has the potential to augment our ability to solve optimization problems, identifying practical performance benefits over classical methods remains an active area of research.\n"
msgstr ""
"Quantum optimization menjelajahi bagaimana komputasi kuantum bisa dipakai untuk memecahkan masalah optimisasi, di mana tujuannya adalah menemukan solusi terbaik, atau yang bagus, di antara banyak alternatif yang mungkin (sering kali dengan sekumpulan batasan). Aplikasi bidang ini mencakup logistik dan penjadwalan, optimisasi portofolio, dan protein folding.\n"
"Pendekatan quantum optimization mencakup quantum approximate optimization algorithm (QAOA) dan metode hybrid kuantum-klasik lainnya yang menggabungkan prosesor kuantum dengan teknik optimisasi klasik. Meskipun komputasi kuantum berpotensi meningkatkan kemampuan kita memecahkan masalah optimisasi, mengidentifikasi keunggulan performa praktis dibandingkan metode klasik masih menjadi area riset yang aktif.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Solving an optimization problem on a quantum computer generally involves two stages. First, formulate the problem, (for example, as a quadratic unconstrained binary optimization (QUBO) problem, a higher-order binary optimization (HUBO) problem, or a problem with explicit constraints), and map that formulation into quantum operators and circuits. Second, run the resulting circuit on quantum hardware and interpret the measurement results as a candidate solution. The tools on this page support these two stages: the mapping tool helps you move from a problem definition to a quantum-ready representation, and the application functions combine mapping, hardware execution, and classical post-processing into a single managed workflow.\n"
msgstr "Memecahkan masalah optimisasi di komputer kuantum umumnya melibatkan dua tahap. Pertama, rumuskan masalahnya (misalnya, sebagai masalah quadratic unconstrained binary optimization (QUBO), masalah higher-order binary optimization (HUBO), atau masalah dengan batasan eksplisit), lalu petakan rumusan itu ke operator dan circuit kuantum. Kedua, jalankan circuit yang dihasilkan di hardware kuantum dan tafsirkan hasil pengukuran sebagai kandidat solusi. Tool di halaman ini mendukung kedua tahap tersebut: tool pemetaan membantumu berpindah dari definisi masalah ke representasi yang siap untuk kuantum, dan application functions menggabungkan pemetaan, eksekusi hardware, dan post-processing klasik menjadi satu alur kerja terkelola.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mapping tools {#mapping-tools}"
msgstr "Tool pemetaan {#mapping-tools}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This capability specializes in mapping domain problems into quantum operators and circuits for execution on a quantum computer. Use it to formulate an optimization problem as a binary model, convert that model between representations, and validate it against classical solvers before running on quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr "Kemampuan ini mengkhususkan diri dalam memetakan masalah domain ke operator dan circuit kuantum untuk dieksekusi di komputer kuantum. Pakai ini untuk merumuskan masalah optimisasi sebagai model biner, mengonversi model itu antar representasi, dan memvalidasinya dengan solver klasik sebelum dijalankan di hardware kuantum.\n"

